  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lmi Consulting obligated $418M in FY2026 to date across 71 awards, with an average award size of $5.9M and obligations up 21.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $1.1M in FY21 to $418M in FY26, with intermediate totals of $199M in FY22, $219M in FY23, $394M in FY24, and $343M in FY25. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $214M, followed by General Services Administration at $109M and Department of Defense at $58.6M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest market at $240M, followed by Engineering Services at $125M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $20.1M. Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Veterans Affairs, and NASA also appear among buyers with obligations of $26M, $7.1M, and $1.8M respectively. Computing and other IT-related markets account for smaller shares, including $499K in Computing Infrastructure Providers and $264K in Other Computer Related Services. Current-year totals are partial and reported fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies buy the most from Lmi Consulting?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security obligated $214M from Lmi Consulting in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration obligated $109M and Department of Defense obligated $58.6M. Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Veterans Affairs, and NASA follow with $26M, $7.1M, and $1.8M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets drive Lmi Consulting revenue?",
        "body": "Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services drove $240M in obligations for Lmi Consulting in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services provided $125M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences provided $20.1M. Smaller market contributions include Landscape Architectural Services at $16.4M and Office Administrative Services at $15.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
